 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items?limit=<n>&cursor=<token>` →
+  `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": <token-or-null>}`: items are ordered by
+  `id`. `limit` is optional (default `20`, range `1`–`100`). Pass a returned
+  `next_cursor` unchanged to fetch the next page; it is `null` on the last
+  page. Invalid limits and cursors return status 400 with `{"error": "..."}`.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
